+# V2 Loop Routing and Resume Implementation Plan
+
+> **For Claude:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.
+
+**Goal:** Port multi-provider routing, tier-aware model selection, resume with gap analysis, topological gate re-queue, and prompt budget shaping into the v2 spec loop.
+
+**Architecture:** Five capabilities are added to the v2 loop layer. A new `internal/v2/routing/` package owns provider selection and tier resolution. The bead loop and spec loop become the routing seam — they call `Router.Select()` before each stage invocation and populate `StageRequest.Provider` and `StageRequest.Model`. Stages remain stateless. The prompt assembler gains budget shaping. Resume logic lives in the spec loop as orchestration (not a stage).
+
+**Tech Stack:** Go 1.24, existing v2 packages, no new external dependencies
+
+---
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Components
+
+1. **`internal/v2/routing/`** (new package)
+   - `Router` struct — 3-layer provider selection (phase preferences, ratio balancing, fallback with cooldown)
+   - `tier.go` — tier resolution from config (`PhaseModelTier`, `BuildTierForStrategy`, `NextEscalationTier` delegation)
+   - `Provider` interface — wraps `llmtypes.LLMProvider` with `Name()` and `ModelForTier(tier)` methods
+
+2. **`internal/v2/stage/stage.go`** (modified)
+   - `StageRequest` gains `Provider llmtypes.LLMProvider` field
+
+3. **`internal/v2/loop/bead_loop.go`** (modified)
+   - Routing seam: call `Router.Select(phase, tier)` before each stage, populate `StageRequest.Provider` and `Model`
+   - Escalation: on retry, increment tier via `NextEscalationTier()`, re-call `Router.Select()`
+   - Gate re-queue: when gate returns `DecisionBlock`, re-queue bead (already partially implemented via `errBeadBlocked`)
+
+4. **`internal/v2/loop/spec_loop.go`** (modified)
+   - Resume: gap analysis + selective revalidation before bead loop on resume
+   - Routing seam for spec-level stages (plan, decompose, accept)
+
+5. **`internal/v2/prompt/assembler.go`** (modified)
+   - `Assemble(phase string, fileCount int)` — budget-aware assembly
+   - Phase-filtered rules, scoped CLAUDE.md, scope-adjusted budgets
+   - `ShapeReport` for observability
+
+6. **`internal/v2/remediation/remediation.go`** (modified)
+   - `Run(ctx, specID, worktree string)` — expanded signature for worktree propagation
+
+7. **`cmd/gromit/run2.go`** (modified)
+   - Construct `Router` from `cfg.Providers` and `cfg.Routing`
+   - Pass router to spec loop and bead loop
+
+### Data Flow
+
+```
+run2.go: construct Router from config
+  → SpecLoop.Run(): Router.Select(phase, tier) for plan/decompose/accept
+    → resume: gap analysis → selective revalidation → modified bead list
+    → BeadLoop.Run(): Router.Select(phase, tier) per stage per bead
+      → on retry: NextEscalationTier() → Router.Select() with higher tier
+      → on gate block: re-queue bead (already implemented)
+      → PromptAssembler.Assemble(phase, fileCount) → budget-shaped prompt
+```
+
+### Integration Points
+
+- Router is constructed in `run2.go` and passed to loops via new option functions
+- Stages use `req.Provider.Invoke()` if non-nil, falling back to their constructed provider
+- `PromptAssembler` is called by `run2_components.go` stage constructors with phase awareness
+- Resume gap analysis runs in spec loop before bead loop starts
+
+---
+
+## Test Strategy
+
+- **Unit tests** for each new package/function in isolation with table-driven tests
+- **Integration tests** for routing seam in bead loop (mock router + mock stages)
+- **Mock strategy**: Define mock `LLMProvider` and mock `Router` for test injection
+- **Coverage**: Every acceptance criterion from the spec has a corresponding test
+- All tests use `t.Chdir()` (not `os.Chdir()`), `t.Cleanup()` for injectable var restoration
